# Cloud agents
- Default for repo-bound TravelAgency work: code, tests, analysis, architecture/wiki draft text, CI/Docker file edits, deep PR review. Goal: keep the lead chat thin (full brief in, PR or short report out). Do it yourself for work needing server, secrets, chat history, live owner talk, merge, board, or wiki publish. Never both.
- Launch: check no branch/PR/agent exists for the issue; one issue, one agent; branch `type/NN-short-english-slug` via `gh issue develop <NN> --name type/NN-short-english-slug --base main` when the branch does not exist yet (`linkedBranches` only, no closedBy); attach this repo's rules (they are in `.cursor/`, the agent reads them). Prompt in English with the brief below. Keep it short (about 10-20 lines) and include every item.
- No usage-mode matrix and no scheduled limits refresh (unified Cursor subscription, Oct 28, 2026). Prefer cloud whenever a brief covers the task and the result should not live in lead memory.
- Model: default Grok, medium effort (low mechanical, high multi-file/auth/security, xhigh hard). Opus only if Grok xhigh failed or the task is big and critical; state why.
- Cloud agent rules: regular PR into `main`, never push to `main`, never merge, never edit wiki/board, no secrets or server access. In the PR «Задача» section link `#NN` only; never write `closes`/`fix`/`fixes`; do not call `addCloseIssueReferences`. Link the issue to the branch with `gh issue develop` when creating the branch (`project-github-formats.mdc`). Do not move Projects columns. Mark PR ready when CI is green. Final report (English): PR URL, head sha, what changed, tests added, open doubts.
- Acceptance: the launcher owns the result. Strip Cursor PR-body markers and the «Open in Cursor» footer (`gh pr edit --body-file`). Fixes via reply to the same agent. Then merge gates: CI and Cursor Automations have finished, every open finding has a finished reply, and step 6 escalation is done when it triggers (`project-cursor-automations.mdc`, `playbook-step-06-review.mdc`).

## Orchestrator loop (lead; do not skip)
The lead stays the controller after every cloud agent. Cloud agents do not self-merge, self-accept on dev, or talk to the owner.

The loop is the lead↔cloud-agent control microcycle for each workflow step (1-8). It does not replace the `playbook-workflow.mdc` hierarchy (Roadmap → Epic → Feature → Subtask) or steps 1-8. Code (step 5) starts only when steps 1-4 are on the Feature page («полное ТЗ»). The epic page is upper-level analysis, not that TZ. Bugs and small fixes skip 1-4 per workflow.

1. **Pick and arm:** take next Очередь item (`project-github-formats.mdc` «Queue priority»); set `статус: в работе`; determine which step is due (1-4 wiki sections vs 5 code) and which level applies («Analysis depth» in `playbook-workflow.mdc`). Do not launch step 5 if steps 1-4 are missing on the Feature page. Bugs and small fixes skip 1-4. Do not treat the epic page as the screen TZ. Record `Waiting on` / `Next` in `pipeline.md` when the task waits on CI, Deploy, or a cloud agent.
2. **Brief and launch:** one issue, one agent, full brief (`## Brief` below). For wiki/analysis steps: agent returns ready Russian text that meets the step file for that level (step 1: `playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc`, epic blocks or full feature blocks, no architecture); lead reviews then publishes. For code: agent opens the PR.
3. **On result (review, do not redo):** strip Cursor PR markers/footer; check diff vs acceptance criteria and issue scope (no drive-by); formats and secrets (`playbook-git-pr.mdc`, `00-core.mdc`); open doubts from the agent report. Never re-implement the same work in chat.
4. **Steer:** gaps or CI/automation findings → `reply` to the **same** agent with a concrete fix ask; wait for the new head. Wrong agent or obsolete run → cancel/archive; do not leave orphan PRs or agents without an owner and a next step.
5. **Coordinate:** parallel streams only per `project-travelagency.mdc` «Parallel work»; pipeline.md is the single in-flight map. One owner per task; do not hand the same issue to two agents.
6. **Gates then merge:** step 6 (`playbook-step-06-review.mdc`) then merge order; notify the owner after merge.
7. **Live acceptance and docs:** step 7 on dev (lead); step 8 Doc-/ADR (cloud draft OK, lead publishes); then `статус: готово` and close. Doc- automation gaps stay with the lead.


## Brief (required)
The launch prompt includes all of the following. Do not paste this file or unrelated project guides.

- Goal and acceptance: what must be true when the work stops. Name the level (`playbook-workflow.mdc` «Analysis depth»). Step 1 is product WHY and WHAT only (`playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc`). Feature code waits for steps 1-4 on the Feature page.
- Links: issue `#NN`, wiki Epic and/or Feature page (+ anchor), related `Doc-` pages for current behavior this task touches, and any comment that already decided the approach.
- Architecture context: for feature or code work, name the parent Epic architecture choices and the applicable project-wide constraints (services, contracts, auth).
- Minimal environment context: only the stack touchpoints this task hits (which service, gateway, frontend, tests, CI, Docker). Not the whole project guide. Stack touchpoints do not replace the Epic, Feature, and `Doc-` links above; those links stay in the brief.
- Hard boundaries: no wiki edits, no board changes, no merge; no secrets and no server access; stay inside the issue scope; open a regular PR into `main`.
- Where results go: PR sections from `project-github-formats.mdc` («Что сделано», «Зачем», «Как это работает», «Как проверить», «Задача» with `#NN` only). No «Учебный кейс». No `closes` / `fix` / `fixes`. An issue comment, if one is needed, uses «Итог / Подробно / Дальше» (`.cursor/templates/issue-comment.md`). Public text follows `00-core.mdc`: impersonal Russian; Cursor Automations may be named when the sentence needs a process actor. Do not name a role or another agent as the actor.
- Token thrift: minimal diff, no drive-by refactor, stop when the acceptance criteria hold.
